@startuml analytics-flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
title Enunas — Analytics Flow (Current State + Planned)

actor Admin
actor "Brand Partner" as Brand
participant "Admin Dashboard\nAnalytics Tab" as Dashboard
participant "AdminController\n/admin/**" as AC
participant "CustomerService" as CS
participant "ReconciliationService" as RS
participant "LedgerService" as LS
participant "ProductAnalytics\nRepository" as PAR
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

note over Dashboard
  Current state (MVP):
  - Analytics tab in admin dashboard: Phase 2 "Coming Soon"
  - Customer spending analytics: implemented via AdminController
  - Financial reconciliation: implemented
  - Product analytics entity exists (ProductAnalytics) but no dedicated analytics API

  Planned (Phase 2):
  - Full analytics dashboard for admin
  - Vendor analytics dashboard
  - Revenue trends, product performance
end note

' ─── Customer Spending Analytics (IMPLEMENTED) ────────────────────

group Customer Spending Analytics (Admin Only — Implemented)

  Admin -> Dashboard : Opens Customers tab → Select customer → View analytics
  Dashboard -> AC : GET /admin/customers/{id}/spending
  AC -> CS : getCustomerBrandSpending(customerId)

  CS -> DB : SELECT\n  order_items.brand_snapshot_name,\n  SUM(order_items.line_total) as totalSpent,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT orders.id) as orderCount\nFROM orders\nJOIN order_items ON orders.id = order_items.order_id\nWHERE orders.buyer_id = :customerId\n  AND orders.status IN ('PAID','SHIPPED','DELIVERED')\nGROUP BY brand_snapshot_name
  DB --> CS : [ { brandName: "Oma Kulture", totalSpent: 389.00, orders: 2 }, ... ]
  CS --> Admin : Brand spending breakdown per customer

end

' ─── Financial Reconciliation Analytics (IMPLEMENTED) ────────────

group Financial Reconciliation — Drift Detection (Admin Only — Implemented)

  Admin -> AC : GET /admin/reconciliation
  AC -> RS : checkReconciliation()
  RS -> DB : SELECT\n  brand_partner_id,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN status='PENDING_RELEASE' THEN brand_payout ELSE 0 END) AS expected_pending,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN status='AVAILABLE' THEN brand_payout ELSE 0 END) AS expected_available\nFROM ledger_entries\nGROUP BY brand_partner_id

  RS -> DB : SELECT brand_partner_id, pending_balance, payout_balance\n  FROM brand_economics

  RS -> RS : Compare expected (from ledger) vs actual (from brand_economics)
  alt No drift
    RS --> Admin : { all_brands: "OK" }
  else Drift detected
    RS --> Admin : { brandId: 42, expected: 1200.00, actual: 1180.00, drift: 20.00 }
  end
end

' ─── Payout Dashboard Analytics (IMPLEMENTED) ────────────────────

group Payout Dashboard — Financial Status (Admin Only — Implemented)

  Admin -> AC : GET /admin/payouts/dashboard
  AC -> CS : getPayoutDashboard()

  CS -> DB : SELECT status, COUNT(*) as count, SUM(amount) as total\n  FROM payouts GROUP BY status
  DB --> CS : [\n  { status: PENDING, count: 3, total: 2340.00 },\n  { status: APPROVED, count: 1, total: 890.00 },\n  { status: PAID, count: 12, total: 8420.00 }\n]

  CS -> DB : SELECT brand_partner_id, outstanding_debt\n  FROM brand_economics WHERE outstanding_debt > 0
  DB --> CS : Brands with negative balance (debt)

  CS --> Admin : Dashboard { pending: {...}, approved: {...}, paid: {...}, debtAlerts: [...] }
end

' ─── Product Analytics Entity (EXISTS, NO API) ───────────────────

note over PAR
  ProductAnalytics entity exists in the codebase:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  product_analytics table:
    - product_id (FK)
    - view_count
    - purchase_count
    - revenue_generated
    - last_purchased_at

  Currently: entity is created with each product
  (CASCADE from Product).

  No API endpoint reads or writes ProductAnalytics data.
  No service method populates view_count or purchase_count.

  Implementation path for Phase 2:
  1. Track view events on GET /products/{id}
     → increment view_count
  2. Track purchase events in OrderService.confirmPaymentByWebhook()
     → increment purchase_count, revenue_generated
  3. Expose via GET /admin/analytics/products
  4. Expose via GET /brand/analytics/products (own products only)
end note

' ─── Customer Behavior Analytics (NOT IMPLEMENTED) ───────────────

note over Dashboard
  Phase 2 Analytics — NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Admin Analytics Dashboard:
    - Revenue trends (daily/weekly/monthly)
    - Order volume by status
    - Top-selling products and brands
    - Customer acquisition funnel
    - Return rate analysis
    - Commission revenue tracking
    - Geographic distribution

  Brand Analytics Dashboard:
    - Own product view/purchase counts
    - Revenue over time
    - Stock depletion rate
    - Customer repeat purchase rate

  Customer Profile Analytics:
    - Purchase frequency
    - Average order value
    - Category preferences vs purchases

  Required infrastructure additions:
    - Analytics event log table OR
    - Dedicated analytics service (e.g., Mixpanel, PostHog) OR
    - SQL aggregation views on existing order/ledger tables
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
end note

@enduml
